      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Whose turn, and is it done?"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "**Tocar** works like gustar: **me toca**, **te toca**, **le toca** + infinitive. Hoy **te toca** limpiar el baño. For emphasis: **te toca a ti**.\n\nTo ask whether something is done, use the perfecto with **ya** and **todavía no**.\n\n- ¿**Has sacado** la basura? — **Ya la he sacado.** / **Todavía no la he sacado.**\n\nThe pronoun **lo, la, los, las** goes before **he**: los platos → **los** he lavado; la cama → **la** he hecho.\n\nThree irregular participles do most of the work: **hecho** (hacer), **puesto** (poner), **roto** (romper).\n\nThe result takes **estar**: la cocina **está limpia**; el baño **está sucio**."
      }
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": {"en": "A dirty kitchen"},
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "La cocina está muy sucia. ¿Has lavado los platos?",
          "en": "The kitchen is very dirty. Have you washed the dishes?",
          "analisis": [
            ["La cocina", "subject"],
            ["está", "verb"],
            ["muy sucia", "description"],
            ["¿Has lavado", "verb"],
            ["los platos", "object"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Todavía no los he lavado. Pero ya he hecho la cama.",
          "en": "I haven't washed them yet. But I've already made the bed.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Todavía no", "not yet"],
            ["los he lavado", "verb"],
            ["ya", "already"],
            ["he hecho", "verb"],
            ["la cama", "object"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Hoy te toca a ti limpiar el baño.",
          "en": "Today it's your turn to clean the bathroom.",
          "analisis": [["Hoy", "time"], ["te toca a ti", "verb"], ["limpiar el baño", "subject"]]
        },
